<title>USA: Western Country Clubs head in talks to sell stake.</title>
<headline>Western Country Clubs head in talks to sell stake.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Western Country Clubs Inc president Troy Lowrie said he is in talks with a group of individuals regarding the sale of a &quot;substantial portion&quot; of his shares in the company.</p>
<p>Speaking in a press release, Lowrie said the proposed buyers are persons who have experience in managing and owning businesses similar to Western.</p>
<p>The proposed sale is contingent on certain conditions including a $7,000,000 firm commitment from an underwriter.</p>
<p>--New York Newsdesk 212 859 1610</p>
</text>
